A||||3||ponya||Oil pan screws||||1||
Z||000000||ponya||06-21-2000||11:15 PM||||I'll try to make this short. I am going to change my oil pan gasket this weekend. I have an 86/w 2.8 V-6. I read that there are different size bolts in this pan. How many different I don't know. They also say that they have to be in the right slots. Can someone tell me how many different size bolts there are and does someone have a schematic on what bolt goes where. Service manual does not show it.  Any help, thanks, Bob||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||06-22-2000||09:09 PM||||I can't remember exactly cause I did my gasket last Oct, but I do remember laying them in such a way I wouldn't "screw" them up when putting them back in <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Just draw yourself a map if you have to. Number the holes on the map, then laying the bolts in order on the map.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-22-2000||09:13 PM||||Assuming GM followed the usual rules.....<P>they are all the same size or there are 2 sizes.<P>If they are 2 sizes:<P>4 larger ones go near the main seals.<P>the rest are smaller and go in all the remaining holes along each side.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DiggityDan||06-22-2000||09:22 PM||||On my 85 V6, there are only two bolts that are different. The ones at the rear main are just a little longer than the rest of them. I know they changed the oil pan/timing chain cover design but I think that was in 87 so yours should be the same.||||reg||1
